# SNOW-LAYER (FIELD-WINTER p13): the world's snow is a Surface Layer graph asset (ShaderGraph Domain SurfaceLayer,
# Common/SurfaceLayer.glslh). WP_Winter names ShaderGraphs/M_SnowLayer.dgraph (the p12 look, now authored as a graph:
# Snow010A textures, SnowCover threshold, relief drift); WP_Winter_Dirty names M_SnowLayer_Dirty.dgraph (the same snow
# + the stony_dirt_path scan in blotches masked by the snow scan's relief at a 13 m repeat). The layer is picked by a
# world parameter value, so the switch below is the next frame, not a restart or a recompile.
Дано run Scene "Open Scene FIELD_Barn_Winter.desce"
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано run Entity "Sun"
Дано --subject selection set SunElevation 25
Дано --subject selection set SunAzimuth 110
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position -300,2221,-3600
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction -0.53,-0.51,-0.7
Тогда-вид 1_snow_layer snow as 3_winter_tree p12: crowns white on top as a layer, undersides and trunks green/dark, the ground and the barn roof white; editor.log has no shader compile error
Когда set world SceneSettings.WorldParameters assets:WorldParameters/WP_Winter_Dirty.dworldparams
Тогда-вид 2_snow_dirty the same view, the snow now with brown-grey dirt patches metres across on the ground, the crowns' snow and the roof carry the same layer; no restart; editor.log has no shader compile error
